--------------------------------------------
#include "mnist_hls.h"

/* Dump your trained values here.
 * Example: { 0.03125, -0.01758, 0.00671, … } */
const data_t W1[N_H1][N_IN] = { /* 128 x 784 numbers */ };
const data_t B1[N_H1]       = { /* 128             */ };

const data_t W2[N_H2][N_H1] = { /*  64 x 128 numbers */ };
const data_t B2[N_H2]       = { /*  64             */ };

const data_t W3[N_OUT][N_H2] = { /* 10 x 64 numbers */ };
const data_t B3[N_OUT]       = { /* 10            */ };

------------------------------------------------
HLS directives in a glance
------------------------------------------------
1. m_axi ‑ image pixels fetched through a burst AXI-4 master.  
2. s_axilite –  the PS (ARM) configures / starts the accelerator.  
3. PIPELINE   – inner loops run with II = 1, one MAC per clock.  
4. ARRAY_PARTITION – keeps small vectors in registers for parallel MACs.  
5. The weight matrices are declared const so the tool maps them to ROMs.

